WEBVTT

00:00:00.566 --> 00:00:07.328
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Sidney Poitier was the first black person to win the Best Actor Oscar in 1964

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.359
for his performance in <i>Lilies of the Field</i>.

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:18.351
Denzel Washington was the second black man to win the Best Actor Oscar in 2002 for <i>Training Day</i>.

00:00:19.208 --> 00:00:25.484
He described Poitier as ‘the man who opened doors for us that had been closed for years.’

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.714
Sidney Poitier was the youngest of seven children.

00:00:35.319 --> 00:00:38.807
His parents were tomato farmers who worked in the Bahamas,

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.975
where they had no running water or electricity.

00:00:43.011 --> 00:00:47.049
He was born two months early and nobody expected him to live.

00:00:47.723 --> 00:00:51.683
His mother went to see a fortune-teller to find out if he would survive.

00:00:52.259 --> 00:00:55.208
She said, ‘Don't worry about your son.

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.050
He will carry your name to many places.’

00:00:58.914 --> 00:01:05.700
At 16, with no education, Sidney arrived in New York with only $3 in his pocket.

00:01:06.201 --> 00:01:11.693
He tried to get a job as an actor, but the director told him, ‘Stop wasting your time.

00:01:11.999 --> 00:01:13.866
Get a job as a dishwasher.’

00:01:14.723 --> 00:01:18.986
He was married twice, to a dancer, with whom he had four daughters,

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:22.747
and to a Canadian actor, with whom he had two daughters.

00:01:23.662 --> 00:01:28.655
In his 50 years in film, he starred in and directed 40 films.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.551
He played many iconic roles,

00:01:31.714 --> 00:01:39.216
including a young doctor in <i>Guess Who’s Coming to Dinner</i> and a teacher in <i>To Sir, With Love</i>.

00:01:40.319 --> 00:01:45.771
He received many awards, including a knighthood from Queen Elizabeth II

00:01:46.065 --> 00:01:54.254
and an Honorary Oscar in recognition of his ‘remarkable accomplishments as an artist and as a human being.’

00:02:05.857 --> 00:02:08.760
Denzel Washington was born in New York.

00:02:09.623 --> 00:02:14.756
His mother owned a beauty parlour, and his father was a church minister.

00:02:15.685 --> 00:02:21.772
His parents divorced when he was 14, and his mother sent him to an expensive private school.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:27.530
He later went to university and got a degree in drama and journalism.

00:02:28.571 --> 00:02:32.084
At a time when Denzel wasn’t doing well at university,

00:02:32.341 --> 00:02:36.379
a woman told his mother that she had a prophecy about her son.

00:02:36.839 --> 00:02:41.639
She said that he ‘would travel the world and speak to millions of people’.

00:02:42.531 --> 00:02:45.380
He has been married since 1983,

00:02:45.577 --> 00:02:51.384
and he and his wife Pauletta have four children, two sons and two daughters.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:58.595
He has played many Shakespeare roles since his early days as an actor, both in theatre and film,

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:05.351
including Lord Macbeth in Joel Coen’s 2021 film <i>The Tragedy of Macbeth</i>.

00:03:06.539 --> 00:03:08.552
He has received many awards,

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:14.604
including an Oscar for Best Supporting Actor for his role in the film <i>Glory</i>.